{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae","id":53897,"title":"Dark Ages: Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-20T05:02:03-08:00","id":53897,"title":"Dark Ages: Fae","content":"I just read this book and after years and years of hating ANYTHING C:TD related (sorry, it just doesn't appeal to me) I have to say.... WOW. I really like what they did with it and how it evolved.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that if C:TD had been like DA:F I would have really gotten into it all those years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:51:25-08:00","id":54031,"title":"","content":"Ditto. I loved that book as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:38:30-08:00","id":54262,"title":"","content":"I wish Changeling magic still worked as well as it does in Dark Ages and not the haphazard way it seems to be put together in the Dreaming books. I'm still trying to homebrew a rules set for magic in Changeling that makes it a little more flexible the way Mage's magic system is handled. For being creatures of living magic, their powers sure are rigidly structured and limited.<br /> <br /> I concure it is a fantastic book and I used to hate wading through Dark Ages worlds. So Changeling DA was a gateway book for me too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:50:54-08:00","id":54276,"title":"","content":"I really hope that they can expand on fae. I would love to have more books for it. It is distinct from both dreaming and Lost and deserves more books. <br /> <br /> thankfully a section of darkening skies will cover fae IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:51:58-08:00","id":54277,"title":"","content":"well can't you take DA:F and just port it to modern times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:54:39-08:00","id":54280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae?p=54277#post54277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well can't you take DA:F and just port it to modern times?</div> </div> </div> </div>Working on that bit, but it still needs some tweaks. The Mage system would still mop the floor with any Changeling cast spell. Trying to give it more OOMPH without making Changelings completely twinkified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:04:29-08:00","id":54329,"title":"","content":"Well, given that Mages are all, &quot;Reality, you're my bitch,&quot; and changelings are all, &quot;We're Dreams,&quot; it kinda makes sense (IMNSHO) that mages are much, much more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T06:11:06-08:00","id":54624,"title":"","content":"Ehhh... More like Mages say &quot;Reality you're my Bitch&quot; and Reality smacks them back with &quot;Bitch, Please...&quot; I wouldn't call that entirely accurate. While Changelings are More &quot;I reject your reality and substitute my own! Kazam! Enchantment biotch.&quot; It stands to reason that both forms should be a bit more on an equal footing even if Magi are more effective in altering reality for the masses than Changelings are. I've always seen the Banity and the Mists as their main weaknesses. They can be beings of Pure magickal power drawing energy for their spells out of seemingly nothing where Magi need a node or source of tass to do the same. Fae make it look so simple. Banality and the fact even their own powers don't last more than a handful of years keeps them from being more powerful than Magi. However quirks in Changeling's magic system hobble them even further it almost seems like overkill. An opponent can practically face down a Changeling throwing a fireball at them, shut their eyes and yell &quot;This is not happening!&quot; and it just won't. The Changeling gets hit with Banality and depending on how much Glamour they have is dealt a mortal bow with just a few words. Whereas a Mage in the same situation may get serious Paradox, but the guy will still be toast. The Mage framework for Magic is well made and flexible. The Fae Framework is broken.<br /> <br /> Take Ledgermain. At Level 1, Gimmix, you can move an object based on the first set of successes to determine weight you are allowed to lift and throw, then you have to roll more successes to keep it going if say you're trying to lift a person in the air. Or you could try and throw something really heavy at someone else for only up to 4 health levels of damage. Does a higher level in this Art mean you can move bigger stuff easier? No. Just 1 set of successes for what you can move. (and why is 1 success JUST 6 OUNCES?!? WHo Wants to Lift and move Just 6 ounces???) In Mage you can get the same effect using Correspondence 2 for small things in a relatively unlimited range. Level 3 and a Mage can get anything just about anywhere. You don't get limited with 'well you just move stuff' it takes levels of geographical know how into account and gives the Mage the entire field to work with.<br /> <br /> What's more, you can combine spheres in Mage, you can't combine Arts, only Realms. None of the Arts levels seem to be closely related to each other. Mage Spheres takes a concept and builds on it. Primal has you talk to anything first, then next level you get to make a cubic foot of an element per success of either Earth, Air, Fire, Water or Wood. Level 3 has you growing protective Oak Bark skin and Level 4 lets you hurt someone or heal them (which is just about the only deffensive spell they can cast beside making a cubic foot of fire on someone's head or have more than 5 successes with Gimmix). Last level 5 lets you transform into just about anything you want. One could say 'Oh well, all those powers seem Nature based', and they do indeed, But Nature is a Realm not an Art. That's just part of the confusion. Could say that Primal is the equivalent of the Life Sphere, except Willow Whisper can talk to things that were never alive. It's like trying to roll Life, Prime, and Spirit into one ball and yet you only get 5 spells to make out of those spheres and can only use one trait for each. Ever notice how many powers seem to use nature in one way or another, however none of their powers seems to affect weather? And before a Changeling can even use any of these powers on an enemy you have to know what they are in order to use Actor or Fae at Level 5. Those are some serious handicaps and that's mostly intended for use against their own kind.<br /> <br /> Just looking over the book again, here's a prime example of the WTFness.<br /> <br /> Changeling Core 2nd Edition: Pg 187 Portal Passage<br /> <br /> &quot;Portal passage creates an opening through any barrier,<b> up to 10 ft thick.</b> This portal will generally appear as a normal door (6'x3'), though it may be smaller depending upon the size of the barrier. This portal will pierce any barrier <b>no matter how thick.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> The paragraph in the book goes on talking about limits, ignoring that little paradox right up there.<br /> <br /> At least in DA: Fae they had 4 Dominions based upon the Fae's court of the year. Aside from that there are 5 levels of about 15 Common Cantrips. Each one of those Dominions had 5 levels, but each level had from 5 to up to 11(!) cantrips to choose from with specific instructions that Storytellers and players should create New Cantrips for their chronicle. A lot of the cantrips listed were badass too. Only at level 2 and a Fae can cast a WALL OF FIRE. Or Lesser Elf Shot. That one seems Mighty useful. Changeling Dreaming gives you literally 25 Cantrips to use and no variation or options to make anything different. And to do <i>anything</i> effective with <i>any</i> of them you have to have level 5 in just about all your Realms. How's that for setting the bar high? At least in Mage you get an Arete limit on dice, but honestly, there's so little holding a Mage back other than their own hubris getting themselves blown up with a Paradox Blacklash.<br /> <br /> So to tie up, it's not that Mages are just supposed to be more powerful cuz of their 'Magick'. Their system for magic was just written so much better that it allows for much more power in the system compared to Changeling. For a concept that is supposed to be quite powerful in their own right, their system and magic was poorly designed making them weaker by default.<br /> <br /> Now if dealing with a Changeling was more like dealing with a Marauder, Mages would be shaking in their boots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:50:45-08:00","id":77334,"title":"","content":"I'll start with saying I LOVE this book. I never liked Changeling the Dreaming. They're not fae. They're not even really Changelings. Dark Ages Fae has the right feel. I love everything about this supplement and dearly wish this was the direction they had gone with WoD Changelings from the beginning.<br /> <br /> That said, to comment on the debate currently raging, I've run a rather successful DA Fae/DA Mage crossover game (we actually also had a Nuwisha and an elder Lasombra in the group as well, very strange game in a semi-alternate cosmology) and found that each had notable advantages and disadvantages if you remember to capitalize on all of them. Some are subtle and hard to remember, but if you remember to exploit everyone's flaws, it balances out pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:44:10-07:00","id":144872,"title":"","content":"Sorry if the thread is a bit old for revival, but I wanted to mention that last summer (and I think I talked about it on the white wolf forums back then) I had a DA:Fae character in a VtM game and it went pretty well (I had Day dominion banned flaw so as to prevent me from chucking fireballs everywhere =p). I would love to see a banality system introduced to DA:Fae in a modern game.<br /> <br /> For our home game we just said that after the industrial revolution no new faes/changelings have been born, so they are slowly dying off and generally avoiding risk. My character managed to get embraced though and is now a Tremere with Mytherceria as an extra in-clan discipline merit.<br /> <br /> DA:Fae is one of my top 5 favorite RPG books (across all systems) of all time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:23:38-07:00","id":145143,"title":"","content":"Can I ask you Dark Ages: Fae lovers something?<br /> <br /> What do you actually <i>do</i> in this setting? What significant impact do Fae activities have on the mortal world?<br /> <br /> The book had a few cool concepts, but I was never able to find the actual game in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:28:56-07:00","id":145150,"title":"","content":"Mortals are super important to Dark Ages Fae. They draw their strength from Oaths with humans. So kind of like a Vampire game might be about the Kindred manipulating mortal events to further their interests, Fae might get involved in them to preserve their oaths. Other game angles would be courtly intrigue (similar to DA:V). In fact it's a lot more like Vampire than either WW or Mage are but with slightly different emotions and super fun mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T14:23:48-07:00","id":146026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae?p=145150#post145150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals are super important to Dark Ages Fae. They draw their strength from Oaths with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just did a quick search through my PDF and I didn't find that to be the case with Oaths. Am I missing something? I did see that oaths protect Fae from Echoes, which is something.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if that's the case, DA: Fae can make for some interesting stories. The Fae are trying to prepare for the fall of the Oath-Truce, but these pesky humans with their oaths keep getting in their way. But they need to fulfill those oaths to keep their powers.<br /> <br /> It's neat, I just don't see the mechanics for it - if it even needs mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}